# Code owners.
#
# Replace @OWNER with the GitHub username or team that must approve changes to
# the load-bearing files below. Ordinary gameplay PRs are deliberately NOT
# listed — there is no catch-all `*` rule, so day-to-day work is never gated on
# one person.
#
# `require_code_owner_reviews: true` in scripts/apply-repo-settings.sh is what
# makes this file binding. Without that flag it is only a suggestion GitHub
# renders in the UI.

# The rules agents and reviewers work from.
/CLAUDE.md                        @OWNER

# CI/CD: the six required checks, the preview deployment, the deploy.
/.github/workflows/               @OWNER

# Repo protection and provenance.
/.github/CODEOWNERS               @OWNER
/.github/stamp-build.sh           @OWNER
/scripts/apply-repo-settings.sh   @OWNER

# The environment, and the gate definitions.
/scripts/bootstrap.sh             @OWNER
/scripts/check-constraints.sh     @OWNER
/.claude/                         @OWNER

# Config the gates READ. These are listed for the same reason the workflows
# are: they decide what the gates mean, and no job re-checks them.
#
# .gdlintrc IS the lint gate — adding a rule to its `disable:` list makes
# `lint` pass on code it should reject. project.godot and project.conf carry
# the frame and threading constraints that nothing else in CI re-derives.
/.gdlintrc                        @OWNER
/project.godot                    @OWNER
/project.conf                     @OWNER
